{"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV4stemAA7MXLStemVSgvp","title":"stem","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stem"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStemV","text":"MXLStem"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/stem"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The direction of the stem for this note, if any.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/stem"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stem"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStem","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStemV","text":"MXLStem"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<stem>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/stem":{"title":"stem","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stem","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStem","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStemV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/stem","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/stem","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction of the stem for this note, if any."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"title":"MXLNote","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStem":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstem","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStem","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStem","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stems can be down, up, none, or double. For down and up stems, the position attributes can be used to specify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stem length. The relative values specify the end of the stem relative to the program default. Default values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify an absolute end stem position. Negative values of relative-y that would flip a stem instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortening it are ignored. A stem element associated with a rest refers to a stemlet."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStem","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStem"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}